# A Web Page Word saved declares its own page in an `@page` rule (#1944):
# here Letter with 1" top and bottom and 1.25" side margins, selected by
# `div.WordSection1 {page:WordSection1}`. The import reads it instead of
# #1928's Outlook-like 15 px page. View > Print Layout draws the page
# with those margins. The ruler probe reads the text's inset from the
# page's left and top edges in px at 100%, one more than the margin (as
# `html-page-margins.uit` reads 15 px as 16): 121 for 1.25", 97 for 1".
# The text column is the 576 px body less the same px on each side.

test issue 1944 a word web page keeps its own page margins
  open copy:../fixtures/word-page.htm
  call doc {}
  assert reply.view.layout is web
  call ribbon-click {"tab":"View","command":"ruler"}
  call ribbon-click {"tab":"View","command":"Print Layout"}
  shot window
  call doc {}
  assert reply.view.layout is print
  assert reply.view.zoom is 1
  assert reply.ruler.text_inset is 121
  assert reply.ruler.vtop_inset is 97
  assert reply.flow.text_column.width is 574
